[Applause]  we come to you for one of the truly  iconic stadiums in the NFL  don't you dare look at  Bay Wisconsin no team means more  as a graded gold made their way out of  the historic tunnel they're ready to go  as they get set to match up with the  Miami Dolphins  the Madden series aims to be a  true-to-life representation of the  popular American sport of football and  Madden 19 is refined step forward with  advancements across the board there are  some issues hanging over from past games  and the franchise updates are not as big  and exciting as you might expect but  Madden 19 with it's capable frostbite  engine and it's compelling longshot  story mode remains the best most  complete Madden game to date on the  field  Madden's gameplay has never looked or  handled better and this is due in part  to a new system EA calls real player  motion one of the biggest pieces of this  is the new one cut feature for ball  carriers that allows them to change  direction quickly and with a burst of  speed to get around a defender you can  also perform hesitation moves that can  make a big difference in those crucial  moments when you see an opening or a gap  and it's thrilling to successfully  execute a run establishing the run game  can be critical and it's nice to see  Madden 19 make running responsive fun  and representative of what you see in  real NFL games to balance out the new  tactics for ball carriers Madden 19 adds  a new strafe first mechanic for  defenders that helps you get into  position to stop a big play and in a  further step toward simulating actual  NFL games Madden 19 lets you choose a  custom celebration after a touchdown or  a big defensive play with individual and  team based options it gives Madden a  more authentic feel  field and score on the opening drive  on the presentation side Madden 19 uses  the frostbite engine again to great  effect character models are now more  lifelike while small things like player  sweat the way bodies crunch and recoil  after big hits sunspots pouring onto the  field at dusk and weather elements like  rain and snow get even closer to  replicating real life the graphics look  better but the physics can still be  really weird at times arms Bend in ways  they shouldn't character models fuse  together and seeing the crowd jump in  unison can be really strange on the  brighter side the menus have been  updated and now are sleeker and less  cluttered Madden 19's commentating is a  big bright spot thanks to excellent  performances by the play-by-play and  Colour duo of Brandon Gordon and Charles  Davis their banter succeeds thanks to  their football acumen as well as their  ability to emulate real NFL broadcast  booths and shoot the breeze on seemingly  random topics you'll hear at least one  Seinfeld reference be very careful about  what speed they're going to play my  music teacher back in New Paltz misses  my favorite bag Lisa said don't go  prestissimo  [Applause]  when you really want to go at a nice  slow deliberate pace I am speechless I  am without speech Madden 19's commentary  will be updated on a regular basis with  new dialogue lines that reflect what  happens in the real NFL once the season  kicks off later this month however it  remains to be seen if the commentators  will tackle controversial subjects like  the kneeling policy or other current  events  Madden's commentary is known for getting  stale so I hope the new lines are  substantial and fun to listen to another  big part of Madden is the franchise mode  last year's game was frustratingly light  on advancements and improvements there  are some new tweaks this year though  they might not resonate with everyone  one of the more notable new features is  what's called the archetype progression  system this adds different styles to  positions unless you continue to build  and expand your players over the course  of one or multiple seasons the XP you  earn in games gives you skill points  that you can then spend to upgrade one  of the archetypes for your player  instead of assigning them to specific  attributes as you could in previous  games this can feel frustrating as it  effectively limits the amount of fine  control you have to shape your players  another way to play Madden is through  the card based madden ultimate team mode  and it's stocked with things to do this  year in addition to the standard  challenges of which there are more than  100 there are solo battles where you can  go up against other fan-created mutt  squads in weekly tournaments well there  will also be a playlist for mutt squads  made by EA SPORTS developers NFL players  and celebrities it's a thrill to take on  a different squad each playthrough in  solo battles and I can see myself  returning again and again to this mode  to see how my team stacks up already a  deep and robust mode mutt adds the brand  new mutt squad challenges where you and  two others take on the CPU in a series  of online football challenges provided  your teammates know what they're doing  this is a mode that delivers yet another  compelling reason to play mutt online  and keep coming back madden ultimate  team still pushes you towards  microtransactions and that may be a  concern for some but it remains as  exciting and satisfying as ever to put  together a fantasy team where Tom Brady  could throw a touchdown pass to Jerry  Rice it's been a year now since Wade  made a name for himself on the hit show  long shot but now he's been signed by  the Dallas Cowboys and a year ago I  would have said Wade's got a shot at a  decent NFL career but let's be honest  this last year has been really rough on  him on the story side Madden 19 brings  back the long shot mode which was a  breath of fresh air last year the new  called longshot homecoming picks up with  Devin Wade having a tough time in the  Dallas Cowboys training camp with Colt  Cruz struggling through life in Mathis  and getting blindsided by a major life  event the voice acting and performances  of all the major characters weight in  particular are solid ei also recruited  celebrities like Rob Schneider Ron  Cephas Jones  Jimmy Tatro and Joey King for the mug  and they turn in memorable performances  homecoming story is one of pain and  struggle loss and redemption and how  football really doesn't matter when  compared to issues at home and in life  homecoming  like the original longshot before it has  bold ambitions in terms of the story it  tells and the feelings it wants to evoke  but it doesn't always work out at times  it can be uneven and inconsistent in its  tone coming across as hokey and  ham-handed and in what is a surprising  move ei almost completely dropped the  telltale style dialogue options from the  first iteration it's a real shame that  ei moved away from this in favor of a  more traditionally structured story that  being said the narrative will pull you  through and at just about four hours in  length you may finish it in one sitting  despite a significant difficulty spike  at the end I had a fun time playing  through Devon and Colts story which  reached a satisfying and heartwarming  conclusion Madden 19 is an excellent  football game that improves on last  year's entry in almost every way there  are problems but there has never been a  football game that more authentically  represents the NFL than this in terms of  presentation controls and depth  [Applause]  Derick are taking it in from seven yards  away  and to me that's how I allow you to  start grinning widely on your sideline I  think they pretty much locked this one  away  yeah that's the clencher the proverbial  icing on the cake

